@@ -455,6 +456,12 @@ So a transparent capture must be composited over `#08080a` before the critic run
 transparent plate and the studio plate are then compared on the same pixels. That rule is declared
 now, ahead of the option, so the two cannot arrive in different rounds.
 
+### Eye colour
+
+Optional `eyeColour: 'blue'` selects a fixed blue iris pigment. Omission, `null` or `'original'` retains the exact authored sample path. Other values are rejected before allocation. This choice is fixed for an Avatar and follows eye rebuilds; create a new Avatar to change it. Existing pupil, gaze, refraction, cornea and sclera responsibilities remain. Blue is a colour customization, not a calibrated or physical iris model.
+
+`avatar.report().eyes` observes the requested/applied option, actual globe/cornea attachment, pigment vector and whether attachment and request match. A requested Blue that cannot construct eye shading fails instead of silently falling back. Original retains the existing catch/report policy when eye shading is unavailable; complete construction on a figure without eyes is not qualified here. Showcase offers Original/Blue and Apply; Apply opens a fresh preview and resets orbit, motion and attention. JSON and named saved looks preserve Blue; Original is omitted. Export refuses a mismatched or detached custom eye owner.
+
 ### Hair colour
 
 With a hair style enabled, optional `hairColour: '#765344'` supplies a six-digit sRGB material colour. Uppercase hex is accepted and normalized to lowercase. Named CSS colours, shorthand hex, numeric values, null and colour without a hair style are rejected. Omit the option to retain the exact existing derived default; a rounded hex is not substituted for that default.
